From fb765a6da98cfb9a92afde65b18da60c2dc81c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:58:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 49/58] qsa: tag every raw-key ring row and validate it before
 pooling

The fused pre-indexer could read a stale or uncommitted raw-key ring row and
pass its int64 tail to RoPE as a position (illegal address). The writer now
tags each row with logical_position + 1; the reader checks the tag of every
source row and, on a mismatch, masks the pooled load, the RoPE-tail read and
the compressed-slot store. New guard site 11 (always fatal under warn). The
KV pool size is unchanged.
